{"schemaVersion":3,"targetDevice":"mk2","id":"CM9Vlqn1WiK95frlGOfP","name":"3rd Wave 8M v1.7","description":"\n# Groove Synthesis 3rd Wave 8M with patch parsing and comparison mode\n\n- Synth must be on at least OS 2.0 (August 2026)\n\n- The 8M is a 2-part synth. The preset might work with the 4-part 24M model, but only for up to 2 parts. To use the 24M change the MODEL_BYTE = 0x02 to 0x01 at the top of the Lua code.\n  \n- **IMPORTANT:** In addition to *MIDI param receive* set to CC+NRPN, the preset expects that *MIDI include part in NRPN* is turned on in the global settings.\n\n- The preset has the single and part 1 nrpn parameters sending on MIDI channel 1, and the part 2 parameters sending on channel 2. Change accordingly.\n\n- The preset is built for the factory P and U wavetables. Some adjustment would be needed for other wavetables. DM me.\n\n- To use the start/stop control for the sequencer set the midi clock source to *in: tempo sync*.\n---\n**What's in the preset**\n- Automatic parsing of a patch when a new patch is selected. The **PATCH SELECT** buttons send a program change message before loading the patch data and mapping to the UI controls. \n- Turning the **PATCH NAMES** switch 'on' retrieves all the patch names from all banks. The button should toggle to an 'off' state after all 500 names are read. The patch number fader will then display the patch names when scrolling. This process takes a couple of minutes to complete. The patch names are then stored locally on the E1 and are loaded instantly whenever the E1 loads. If you later change the saved patches on the 3rd Wave or move the preset to a different E1 slot then repeat the process.\n- Only parameters for one part can be viewed and edited a time. Use the **PART VIEW** control to switch between the part 1 and part 2 specific parameters.  \n- Use the **COMPARE** control to switch between an edited sound (and UI) and the original patch sound (and UI). Very useful! \n- Thanks to @oldgearguy there is a touch screen UI for each of the three 6-stage wavetable-envelopes that makes visualizing and editing much easier and more fun. It should largely mimic the dynamic graphic on the 8M screen except only one envelope is shown at a time.  \n- Various buttons and list controls on the first page mimic the selection option buttons on the 3rd Wave's front panel.\n- **Dark blue** controls are global. **White** controls are patch level, and other **colored** controls are part-specific. Controls are hidden when not in use.\n\n----\n**What's not in the preset**\n- Preset parameters do not update when changed on the 3rd Wave. If you edit directly on the 3rd Wave the preset's UI will get out of sync. \n- No wavetable or multi-sample editing or management.\n- No sequencer pattern building.\n- No global settings are parsed. A couple of global parameters (dark blue) can be changed from the preset. \n- No saving of edited patches from the UI.\n\n----\n\n[firmware and manual](https://groovesynthesis.com/support/)\n\n[Github repository](https://github.com/kiwigrass-byte/3rd-Wave)\n\n---\n ","lua":"-- Preset for Groove Synth 3rd Wave 8M\r\n-- September 2026\r\n-- by @kiwigrass\r\n\r\nlocal DEBUG = false\r\n\r\nlocal function dprint(msg)\r\n   if DEBUG then print(msg) end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-------------------------------- Declare Global Constants -----------------------------\r\n-- 3rd wave model id number: 0x01 for 24 voice products, 0x02 for 8 voice\r\nlocal MODEL_BYTE = 0x02\r\n\r\n-- header for 3rd Wave sysEx messages (will recognize either model id byte)\r\nlocal SYSEX_HEADER = {0x00,0x02,0x4A,0x02}\r\n\r\n------------ virtual parameter numbers ----------------\r\nlocal BANK_NUMBER = 10032\r\nlocal PROG_NUMBER = 10033\r\nlocal SELECT_MINUS = 10034\r\nlocal SELECT_IT = 10035\r\nlocal SELECT_PLUS = 10036\r\nlocal PART_SELECT = 10029 -- not nrpn 69 which displays part info on 3rd Wave's screen\r\nlocal COMPARE_IT = 10039\r\nlocal FX1_TYPE = 227\r\nlocal FX2_TYPE = 231\r\n-- UI wavetable params (visible controls), one per oscillator\r\nlocal WT_UI_PARAMS    = {10040, 10041, 10042}\r\n-- Synth wavetable params (actual NRPN-mapped virtual params) stored on hidden page\r\nlocal WT_SYNTH_PARAMS = {102,   103,   104}\r\n-- toggle for part1 and part 2 unison modes\r\nlocal UNISON1_PARAM = 397\r\nlocal UNISON2_PARAM = 398\r\n\r\n-------------- ctrl ids ---------------------\r\n-- program number ctrl id\r\nlocal CTRL_PROG_NUMBER = 3\r\n-- osc control ids\r\nlocal CTRL_PULSE  = {27,28,29}\r\nlocal CTRL_OFFSET = {30,31,32}\r\n-- sync control ids\r\nlocal CTRL_LFO1_SYNC = 226\r\nlocal CTRL_LFO2_SYNC = 329\r\nlocal CTRL_LFO3_SYNC = 227\r\nlocal CTRL_LFO4_SYNC = 228\r\nlocal CTRL_FX1_SYNC = 324\r\nlocal CTRL_FX2_SYNC = 326\r\n-- unison control (exc switch) ids\r\nlocal CTRL_UNISON1 = {60,66,61,63,46}\r\nlocal CTRL_UNISON2 = {412,413,414,415,416}\r\n-- unison toggle control ids\r\nlocal UNISON1_CTRL  = 59\r\nlocal UNISON2_CTRL  = 411\r\n\r\n-- all FX param control ids -- shown/hidden as needed\r\nlocal CTRL_FX1_IDS = {311,312,313,428, 430,431,432} \r\nlocal CTRL_FX2_IDS = {315,316,317,318,319,320,58, 433,434,437,435,436} \r\n\r\n-- Visibility map for CTRL_FX1_IDS and CTRL_FX2_IDS:\r\nlocal FX1_VIS = {\r\n  [7] = {true, false, true, false, true, false, false}, -- leslie \r\n  [8] = {true, false, false, true, false, true, true }, -- ring mod\r\n}\r\nlocal FX2_VIS = {\r\n  [3] = {true, true, true, true, true, false, false, false, false, false, false, true}, -- echoplex  \r\n  [8] = {true, false, true, false, false, false, false, true, false, false, false, false}, -- leslie \r\n  [9] = {true, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, true, true, true, false}, -- ring mod\r\n  [13] = {true, true, true, true, true, true, true, false, false, false, false, false}, -- shimmer reverb\r\n}\r\n\r\n-- slot reference for pulse width control ---\r\nlocal TARGET_SLOT = {4,16,28}\r\n-- slot reference for unison controls\r\nlocal SLOT_UNISON1 = {[60]=20,[66]=21,[61]=22,[63]=23,[46]=24}\r\nlocal SLOT_UNISON2 = {[412]=20,[413]=21,[414]=22,[415]=23,[416]=24}\r\n\r\n-- page references ---\r\nlocal CTRL_PAGE = 1\r\nlocal OSC_PAGE  = 2\r\nlocal W_ENV_PAGE = 6\r\n\r\n-- other constants --\r\nlocal bankTxt={\"B1\",\"B2\",\"B3\",\"B4\",\"B5\"} \r\nlocal authorDate = \"kiwigrass 2026\" \r\n\r\n--  Device information \r\nlocal currentDevice  = devices.get(1)\r\nlocal deviceId = currentDevice:getId()\r\nlocal channel = currentDevice:getChannel ()\r\nlocal port      = currentDevice:getPort ()\r\n\r\ndevices.create(2, \"Part 1\", port, 1)\r\ndevices.create(3, \"Part 2\", port, 2)\r\nlocal part1Channel = devices.get(2):getChannel ()\r\nlocal part2Channel = devices.get(3):getChannel()\r\n\r\n-- events to track\r\nevents.subscribe(PAGES | POTS)\r\n\r\n-- populate the bottom RH screen information display on load\r\ninfo.setText(authorDate)\r\n\r\n-- Tracks how many ticks have passed for the timer.onTick function\r\nlocal amountTicks = 0 \r\n-- Set timer tick rate (e.g., every 200 milliseconds) \r\ntimer.setPeriod(300) \r\n\r\n-- Compare feature caches (key = parNum, value = 14-bit value)\r\nlocal singleBase, part1Base, part2Base = {}, {}, {}\r\nlocal singleEdit, part1Edit, part2Edit = {}, {}, {}\r\n\r\n-- Guard to prevent onChange recursion during repaint\r\nlocal isApplyingCache = false\r\n\r\n-- UB-Xa-reported channels (source of truth when available)\r\nlocal wavePart1Ch = nil\r\nlocal wavePart2Ch = nil\r\nlocal channelsFromSynth = true\r\n\r\n-- initialize number of wavetables by type \r\nlocal ppgNumber = 0\r\nlocal userNumber = 0\r\nlocal analogNumber = 0\r\nlocal sampleNumber = 0\r\n\r\n-- 3rd Wave-reported channel (source of truth when available)\r\nlocal midiChannel = nil\r\n\r\n-- bound to PART_SELECT param\r\nfunction onPartSelectChanged(valueObject, value)\r\n  if midiChannel == nil then return end\r\n  device:setChannel(midiChannel)\r\n  channel = device:getChannel()\r\n  deviceId = device:getId()\r\n  port = device:getPort()\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- initialize sysEx data\r\nlocal sysExPatch = {}   -- sysExPatch[byte] – stored patch data\r\n\r\n-- to store 100 patch names in 5 banks\r\nlocal nameBank = {}   \r\n-- 1 = bank A, 2= bank B, 3 = bank C, 4 = bank D, 5 = bank E \r\nfor y = 1,5 do        \r\n    nameBank[y] = {}\r\n    -- patch numbers 1..100\r\n    for z = 1,100 do  \r\n        nameBank[y][z] = \"\"\r\n    end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Helper: safe controls.get() (pcall-wrapped for deleted/invalid IDs) ────────\r\nlocal function safeGet(id)\r\n  local ok, c = pcall(controls.get, id)\r\n  return ok and c or nil\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Helper: concatenate two arrays. Used for SysEx message construction\r\nlocal function concat(t1, t2)\r\n  local t = {}\r\n  for i=1,#t1 do t[#t+1] = t1[i] end\r\n  for i=1,#t2 do t[#t+1] = t2[i] end\r\n  return t\r\nend\r\n\r\n------------- Persistence helpers for patch-name cache ----------\r\n-- Electra One runtime in this preset:\r\n--   persist(table)\r\n--   recall(table)\r\n-- We persist a tagged flat map and rebuild nameBank on load.\r\n\r\n-- a tag to keep track of versions of patch-banks on the 3rd Wave \r\nlocal PERSIST_TAG = \"3rdWaveProgNamesV1\"\r\n\r\nlocal function makePatchKey(bank, patch)\r\n  return string.format(\"b%d_p%03d\", bank, patch) -- bank 0..4, patch 0..99\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function flattenNameBank(src)\r\n  local flat = {}\r\n  local count = 0\r\n  for b = 1, 5 do\r\n    for p = 1, 100 do\r\n      local v = src[b] and src[b][p] or \"\"\r\n      v = tostring(v or \"\")\r\n      flat[makePatchKey(b, p)] = v\r\n      if v ~= \"\" then count = count + 1 end\r\n    end\r\n  end\r\n  return flat, count\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function inflateNameBank(flat)\r\n  local dst = {}\r\n  local count = 0\r\n  for b = 1, 5 do\r\n    dst[b] = {}\r\n    for p = 1, 100 do\r\n      local v = (flat and flat[makePatchKey(b, p)]) or \"\"\r\n      dst[b][p] = v\r\n      if v ~= \"\" then count = count + 1 end\r\n    end\r\n  end\r\n  return dst, count\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function saveNameBank()\r\n  local flat, count = flattenNameBank(nameBank)\r\n  local payload = {\r\n    _tag = PERSIST_TAG,\r\n    names = flat\r\n  }\r\n  local ok, err = pcall(persist, payload)\r\n  if ok then\r\n    print(string.format(\"nameBank persisted (%d non-empty names)\", count))\r\n  else\r\n    print(\"nameBank persist failed: \" .. tostring(err))\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function loadNameBank()\r\n  local payload = {}\r\n  local ok, err = pcall(recall, payload) -- recall(destinationTable)\r\n  if not ok then\r\n    print(\"nameBank recall failed: \" .. tostring(err))\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n  if payload._tag ~= PERSIST_TAG then\r\n    print(\"nameBank recall: no matching persisted payload tag\")\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n  if type(payload.names) ~= \"table\" then\r\n    print(\"nameBank recall: payload.names missing/invalid\")\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n  local rebuilt, count = inflateNameBank(payload.names)\r\n  nameBank = rebuilt\r\n  print(string.format(\"nameBank restored (%d non-empty names)\", count))\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Debounced/controlled persistence during large scans\r\nlocal nameBankDirty = false\r\nlocal nameBankUpdates = 0\r\nlocal SAVE_EVERY_N_UPDATES = 50 -- tune if desired\r\n\r\nlocal function markNameBankDirty()\r\n  nameBankDirty = true\r\n  nameBankUpdates = nameBankUpdates + 1\r\n  -- periodic checkpoint save during long scans\r\n  if (nameBankUpdates % SAVE_EVERY_N_UPDATES) == 0 then\r\n    saveNameBank()\r\n    nameBankDirty = false\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function flushNameBankIfDirty()\r\n  if nameBankDirty then\r\n    saveNameBank()\r\n    nameBankDirty = false\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- called when preset first loads\r\nfunction preset.onLoad()\r\n  loadNameBank()  -- restore cached patch names first\r\n  pages.display(1)\r\n  refreshUnisonVisibility()\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- called after loading \r\nfunction preset.onReady()\r\n  getWaveCount(nil,1) -- number of wave tables\r\nend\r\n\r\n----------UI formatter functions -----------------\r\n-- format part pan\r\nfunction pan(valueObject,value)\r\n  local control = valueObject:getControl():getId()\r\n  local side =\" L\"\r\n  if (value < 0 ) then \r\n    controls.get(control):setColor (BLUE)\r\n  elseif (value == 0) then\r\n    side = \" Center\"\r\n    controls.get(control):setColor (ORANGE)\r\n  elseif (value > 0) then\r\n    side = \" R\"\r\n    controls.get(control):setColor (RED)\r\n  end\r\n  return(value)\r\nend\r\n \r\nfunction percent (valueObject, value)\r\n    return (string.format (\"%.1f%%\", value/1.27))\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction zeroOne (valueObject, value)\r\n    return (string.format (\"%.2f\", value/127))\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction gain (valueObject, value)\r\n    return (string.format (\"%.0f\", (value/1.27)))\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction displayBpm(valueObject,value)\r\n   return(math.floor(value) .. \" bpm\")\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- FX2 param 2 when type = shimmer reverb (-12 .. + 12)\r\nfunction fx2Param2(valueObject,value)\r\n  local fx2Num = parameterMap.get(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, FX2_TYPE)\r\n  if fx2Num == 13 then -- shimmer reverb\r\n    local control = valueObject:getControl():getId()\r\n    local x = (24*value/255 - 12)\r\n    if (x < 0 ) then \r\n      controls.get(control):setColor (BLUE)\r\n    elseif (x == 0) then\r\n      controls.get(control):setColor (WHITE)\r\n    elseif (x > 0) then\r\n      controls.get(control):setColor (RED)\r\n    end\r\n    return (string.format (\"%.1f\", x))\r\n  else\r\n    return math.floor(value)\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n----------------- create virtual control for wavetable control so control has no dead spots wher ethere aren't wavetables ----------------\r\nlocal wtSyncing = false\r\nlocal wtLastUi = nil\r\nlocal wtLastSynth = nil\r\n\r\nlocal function findIndex(t, v)\r\n  for i = 1, #t do if t[i] == v then return i end end\r\n  return nil\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Real synth ranges (change only these if firmware/library changes)\r\nlocal WT_SEGMENTS = {\r\n  { tag=\"P\", synthStart=0,   count=36 }, -- can be up to 48\r\n  { tag=\"U\", synthStart=128, count=56 }, -- can be up to 64\r\n  { tag=\"A\", synthStart=256, count=7  },\r\n  { tag=\"WM\", synthStart=384, count=1  },\r\n  { tag=\"S\", synthStart=512, count=11 },\r\n}\r\n\r\n-- Build UI starts automatically\r\nlocal function buildUiStarts(segments)\r\n  local ui = 0\r\n  for _,seg in ipairs(segments) do\r\n    seg.uiStart = ui\r\n    seg.uiEnd   = ui + seg.count - 1\r\n    ui = ui + seg.count\r\n  end\r\n  return ui - 1 -- max UI value\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal WT_UI_MAX = buildUiStarts(WT_SEGMENTS)\r\n\r\nlocal function uiToSynth(ui)\r\n  local u = math.floor((ui or 0) + 0.5)\r\n  if u < 0 then u = 0 end\r\n  if u > WT_UI_MAX then u = WT_UI_MAX end\r\n\r\n  for _,seg in ipairs(WT_SEGMENTS) do\r\n    if u >= seg.uiStart and u <= seg.uiEnd then\r\n      return seg.synthStart + (u - seg.uiStart), seg.tag\r\n    end\r\n  end\r\n  return 0, \"P\"\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function synthToUi(sv)\r\n  local s = math.floor((sv or 0) + 0.5)\r\n\r\n  for i,seg in ipairs(WT_SEGMENTS) do\r\n    local s0, s1 = seg.synthStart, seg.synthStart + seg.count - 1\r\n    if s >= s0 and s <= s1 then\r\n      return seg.uiStart + (s - s0), seg.tag\r\n    end\r\n\r\n    -- dead zone clamps to previous segment end\r\n    local nextSeg = WT_SEGMENTS[i+1]\r\n    if nextSeg and s > s1 and s < nextSeg.synthStart then\r\n      return seg.uiEnd, seg.tag\r\n    end\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  if s < WT_SEGMENTS[1].synthStart then return WT_SEGMENTS[1].uiStart, WT_SEGMENTS[1].tag end\r\n  local last = WT_SEGMENTS[#WT_SEGMENTS]\r\n  return last.uiEnd, last.tag\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- wavetable labels\r\nlocal WAVETABLE = {\r\n  -- PPG: 0..35\r\n  [0]=\"Wavetable P00\",\"Wavetable P01\",\"Wavetable P02\",\"Wavetable P03\",\"Wavetable P04\",\"Wavetable P05\",\"Wavetable P06\",\"Wavetable P07\",\"Wavetable P08\",\"Wavetable P09\",\"Wavetable P10\",\"Wavetable P11\",\"Wavetable P12\",\"Wavetable P13\",\"Wavetable P14\",\r\n      \"Wavetable P15\",\"Wavetable P16\",\"Wavetable P17\",\"Wavetable P18\",\"Wavetable P19\",\"Wavetable P20\",\"Wavetable P21\",\"Wavetable P22\",\"Wavetable P23\",\"Wavetable P24\",\"Wavetable P25\",\"Wavetable P26\",\"Wavetable P27\",\"Wavetable P28\",\"Wavetable P29\",\r\n      \"Wavetable P30\",\"Wavetable P31\",\"Wavetable P32\",\"Wavetable P33\",\"VS_0-63\",\"VS_64-127\",\r\n  -- USER: 128..183\r\n  [128]=\"Additive_Bell_17\", [129]=\"HumanVowelSweep\", [130]=\"DrewWave\", [131]=\"GrooveSynthesis-WaveTable_BC\", [132]=\"Flute-Harmonics\", [133]=\"CoolFMDirty-WaveTable_DN\", [134]=\"BID700E-WaveTable_KK\", [135]=\"KnobGrotto6-WaveTable_DN\", [136]=\"Burble-WaveTable_DN\",\r\n  [137]=\"PrimefallOctaveDirty96k-WaveTable_DN\", [138]=\"MultiWave96k-WaveTable_DN\", [139]=\"MetalSweep96k-WaveTable_DN\", [140]=\"ZigZag\", [141]=\"RandomWaves-KK\", [142]=\"CrossoverHMXdirty-WaveTable_DN\", [143]=\"LowSquareSync-WaveTable_DN\",\r\n  [144]=\"RippinStrange-WaveTable_DN\", [145]=\"Buchla208cB-td_KK\", [146]=\"FIIx_Arr1\", [147]=\"Ringshifted96k-WaveTable_DN\", [148]=\"Fairlight_Harmonic_Doodle\", [149]=\"FiveOscComb-WaveTable_DN\", [150]=\"HarmonicSpreadClip-WaveTable_DN\",\r\n  [151]=\"14DirtySweep2_96k-WaveTable_DN\", [152]=\"BarberpoleTurbosaw-WaveTable_DN\", [153]=\"Science_Channel\", [154]=\"Metal_Bubbles\", [155]=\"DrumWaveTables-WaveTable_KK\", [156]=\"Fuzzbomb96k-WaveTable_DN\", [157]=\"Ooo_Aah_Sweep\", [158]=\"Prime_Fall-WaveTable\",\r\n  [159]=\"RingshiftedB96k-WaveTableDN\", [160]=\"KnobGrottoArp16-WaveTable_DN\", [161]=\"Fairlight_Mode1_Loop\", [162]=\"Fairlight_Mode1_Riser\", [163]=\"Ring_Shift_C\", [164]=\"Turbo_Bubbles\", [165]=\"Harmonic_Dirt_Spread\", [166]=\"TurboHamRadio\",\r\n  [167]=\"Addivie_Bell_Lower\", [168]=\"ResVactrolSquare\", [169]=\"208 Easel 76-H-WaveTable\", [170]=\"Keyumay\", [171]=\"Arp_4072_Saw\", [172]=\"Arp_4072_Square\", [173]=\"Buchla296eSpectra5-WaveTable\", [174]=\"Buchla259Dmx7-WaveTable\",\r\n  [175]=\"208c 20-A-WaveTable\", [176]=\"FM_Crush\", [177]=\"Synclav_FM_1\", [178]=\"Dub_Grind\", [179]=\"SineFold\", [180]=\"Big_Bang\", [181]=\"Synclav_5\", [182]=\"Additive_8_Bit\", [183]=\"Harmonic_Aah\",\r\n  -- ANALOG: 256..262\r\n  [256]=\"Sawtooth\",[257]=\"Square\",[258]=\"SuperSaw\",[259]=\"Sine\",[260]=\"-> Pink Noise\",[261]=\"-> Blue Noise\",[262]=\"Triangle\",\r\n  -- SAMPLE: 512..522\r\n  [512]=\"Drums Vinyl Subs&Snares\",[513]=\"Drums Vinyl Cymbals&Toms\",[514]=\"TubeBell\",[515]=\"Marine vocal 3\",[516]=\"mT Kit\",[517]=\"Kalimba\",[518]=\"CowbellNote\",[519]=\"Electric Bass EQ\",[520]=\"808 Kit\",[521]=\"Hanger Drums\",[522]=\"S10\"\r\n}\r\n\r\n-- update names of wavetable controls\r\nfunction waveTableName(valueObject, value)\r\n  local control = valueObject:getControl():getId()\r\n  local u = math.floor((value or 0) + 0.5)\r\n  local s,tag = uiToSynth(u) -- map UI -> synth domain first\r\n  local name = \"Wavetable P00\"\r\n  if s >= 0 and s <= 35 then\r\n    name = WAVETABLE[s] or \"Wavetable P00\"\r\n  elseif s >= 128 and s <= 183 then\r\n    name = WAVETABLE[s] or \"U00\"\r\n  elseif s >= 256 and s <= 262 then\r\n    name = WAVETABLE[s] or \"A00\"\r\n  elseif s == 384 then\r\n    name = \"WM\"\r\n  elseif s >= 512 and s <= 522 then\r\n    name = WAVETABLE[s] or \"S00\"\r\n  end\r\n  controls.get(control):setName(name)\r\nend\r\n-- update values of UI wavetable controls\r\nfunction waveTableFormat(valueObject, value)\r\n  local u = math.floor((value or 0) + 0.5)\r\n  local s,tag = uiToSynth(u) -- map UI -> synth domain first\r\n  if s >= 0 and s <= 35 then\r\n    return string.format(\"P%02d\", s)\r\n  elseif s >= 128 and s <= 183 then\r\n    return string.format(\"U%02d\", s - 128)\r\n  elseif s >= 256 and s <= 262 then\r\n    return string.format(\"A%02d\", s - 256)\r\n  elseif s == 384 then\r\n    return \"W\"\r\n  elseif s >= 512 and s <= 522 then\r\n    return string.format(\"S%02d\", s - 512)\r\n  end\r\n  return \"\"\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- mod matrix destination labels\r\nlocal DESTINATION = {[0]=\"Destination off\",\"osc 1 freq\",\"osc 2 freq\",\"osc 3 freq\",\"osc all freq\",\"osc 1 level\",\"osc 2 level\", \"osc 3 level\",\"osc all level\", \"osc 1 wave env\",\"osc 2 wave env\",\"osc 3 wave env\",\"osc all wave env\",\r\n    \"osc 1 FM amount\", \"osc2 FM amount\",\"osc3 FM amount\", \"osc all FM amount\", \"osc 1 drift\", \"osc 2 drift\", \"osc 3 drift\", \"osc all drift\", \"osc 1 PW\", \"osc 2 PW\", \"osc 3 PW\", \"osc all PW\", \"LPF drive\", \"LPF cutoff\", \r\n    \"LPF resonance\", \"not used\", \"SVF cutoff\",\"SVF resonance\", \"SVF mode\", \"LFO 1 freq\", \"LFO 2 freq\", \"LFO 3 freq\", \"LFO 4 freq\", \"LFO all freq\", \"LFO 1 amount\", \"LFO 2 amount\", \"LFO 3 amount\", \"LFO 4 amount\", \"LFO all amount\", \r\n    \"LPF env amount\", \"amp env amount\",\"env 3 amount\", \"env 4 amount\", \"SVF env amount\", \"wave env amount\", \"all env amount\", \"f-env attack\", \"a-env attack\", \"env 3 attack\", \"env 4 attack\", \"env all attack\", \"f-env decay\",\r\n    \"a-env decay\", \"env 3 decay\", \"env 4 decay\", \"env all decay\", \"f-env sustain\", \"a-env sustain\", \"env 3 sustain\", \"env 4 sustain\", \"env all sustain\", \"f-env release\", \"a-env release\", \"env 3 release\", \"env 4 release\",\r\n    \"env all release\", \"w-env o1/t1\", \"w-env o2/t1\", \"w-env o3/t1\", \"w-env o1/t2\", \"w-env o2/t2\", \"w-env o3/t2\", \"w-env o1/t3\", \"w-env o2/t3\", \"w-env o3/t3\", \"w-env o1/t4\", \"w-env o2/t4\", \"w-env o3/t4\", \"w-env o1/t5\", \"w-env o5/t5\",\r\n    \"w-env o3/t5\", \"w-env o1/t6\", \"w-env o2/t6\", \"w-env o3/t6\", \"w-env o1/p1\", \"w-env o2/p1\", \"w-env o3/p1\", \"w-env o1/p2\", \"w-env o2/p2\", \"w-env o3/p2\", \"w-env o1/p3\", \"w-env o2/p3\", \"w-env o3/p3\", \"w-env o1/p4\", \"w-env o2/p4\",\r\n    \"w-env o3/p4\", \"w-env o1/p5\", \"w-env o2/p5\", \"w-env o3/p5\", \"w-env o1/p6\", \"w-env o2/p6\", \"w-env o3/p6\", \"pan spread\", \"effect 1 mix\", \"effect 1 par 1\", \"effect 1 par 2\", \"effect 1 par 3\", \"effect 2 mix\", \"effect 2 par 1\", \r\n    \"effect 2 par 2\", \"effect 2 par 3\", \"osc 1 fine\", \"osc 2 fine\", \"osc 3 fine\", \"osc all fine\", \"mod 1 amount\", \"mod 2 amount\", \"mod 3 amount\", \"mod 4 amount\", \"mod 5 amount\", \"mod 6 amount\", \"mod 7 amount\", \"mod 8 amount\", \"smpl start time\",\r\n}\r\n-- update names of mod matrix destination controls\r\nfunction destination(valueObject,value)\r\n  local control = valueObject:getControl():getId()\r\n    controls.get(control):setName (DESTINATION[value])\r\nend\r\n-- mod matrix source labels\r\nlocal SOURCE = {[0]=\"Source off\",\"osc 1\",\"osc 2\",\"osc 3\",\"filter envelope\",\"amp envelope\",\"LFO 1\", \"LFO 2\",\"LFO 3\", \"LFO 4\",\"envelope 3\",\"envelope 4\",\"osc1 wave env\", \"osc 2 wave env\", \"osc 3 wave env\", \"PB wheel\", \"Mod wheel\",\r\n    \"velocity\", \"pressure\", \"foot pedal\", \"midi expression\", \"note number\", \"random\", \"DC\", \"noise\", \"audio out\", \"audio in\", \"MPE PB\", \"MPE Y axis\", \"midi breath ctrl\",\r\n}\r\n-- update names of mod matrix source controls\r\nfunction source(valueObject,value)\r\n  local control = valueObject:getControl():getId()\r\n    controls.get(control):setName (SOURCE[value])\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- control visibility of part 1/2 unison params\r\nlocal function setGroupVisible(ids, visible, color, slotMap)\r\n  for _, id in ipairs(ids) do\r\n    if color then controls.get(id):setColor(color) end\r\n    if visible and slotMap and slotMap[id] then\r\n      controls.get(id):setSlot(slotMap[id], CTRL_PAGE)\r\n    end\r\n    controls.get(id):setVisible(visible)\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction refreshUnisonVisibility()\r\n  local part = parameterMap.get(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, PART_SELECT) or 1\r\n  local p1On = (parameterMap.get(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, UNISON1_PARAM) or 0) == 1\r\n  local p2On = (parameterMap.get(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, UNISON2_PARAM) or 0) == 1\r\n  controls.get(UNISON1_CTRL):setVisible(part == 1)\r\n  controls.get(UNISON2_CTRL):setVisible(part == 2)\r\n  setGroupVisible(CTRL_UNISON1, false, BLUE,  nil)\r\n  setGroupVisible(CTRL_UNISON2, false, GREEN, nil)\r\n  if part == 1 and p1On then\r\n    setGroupVisible(CTRL_UNISON1, true, BLUE, SLOT_UNISON1)\r\n  elseif part == 2 and p2On then\r\n    setGroupVisible(CTRL_UNISON2, true, GREEN, SLOT_UNISON2)\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- control visibility of note sync params\r\nfunction showSyncRate1(valueObject,value)\r\n  local visiBool = value == 1 -- show sync rate for lfo 1 if sync is on\r\n  controls.get(CTRL_LFO1_SYNC):setVisible(visiBool) \r\nend\r\nfunction showSyncRate2(valueObject,value)\r\n  local visiBool = value == 1 -- show sync rate for lfo 1 if sync is on\r\n  controls.get(CTRL_LFO2_SYNC):setVisible(visiBool) \r\nend\r\nfunction showSyncRate3(valueObject,value)\r\n  local visiBool = value == 1 -- show sync rate for lfo 3 if sync is on\r\n  controls.get(CTRL_LFO3_SYNC):setVisible(visiBool) \r\nend\r\nfunction showSyncRate4(valueObject,value)\r\n  local visiBool = value == 1 -- show sync rate for lfo 4 if sync is on\r\n  controls.get(CTRL_LFO4_SYNC):setVisible(visiBool) \r\nend\r\nfunction showSyncRateFx1(valueObject,value)\r\n  local visiBool = value == 1 -- show sync rate for fx 1 if sync is on\r\n  controls.get(CTRL_FX1_SYNC):setVisible(visiBool) \r\nend\r\nfunction showSyncRateFx2(valueObject,value)\r\n  local visiBool = value == 1 -- show sync rate for fx 2 if sync is on\r\n  controls.get(CTRL_FX2_SYNC):setVisible(visiBool) \r\nend\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- FX SPEC TABLES\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- FX1 (PARAM_227 type select, PARAM_228 sync, params 324/325/326 plus 345)\r\nlocal FX1_SPEC = {\r\n  [0]  = { name=\"BYPASS\", params={ [1]={label=\"PARAM 1\"}, [2]={label=\"PARAM 2\"}, [3]={label=\"PARAM 3\"},  }},\r\n  [1]  = { name=\"BBD DELAY\", syncParam=228, params={ [1]={label=\"TIME\"}, [2]={label=\"FEEDBACK\"}, [3]={label=\"CUT OFF\"},  }},\r\n  [2]  = { name=\"STEREO DELAY\", syncParam=228, params={ [1]={label=\"TIME\"}, [2]={label=\"FEEDBACK\"}, [3]={label=\"CUT OFF\"},  }},\r\n  [3]  = { name=\"CHORUS\", params={ [1]={label=\"DEPTH\"}, [2]={label=\"RATE\"}, [3]={label=\"TONE\"}, }},\r\n  [4]  = { name=\"PHASER\", params={ [1]={label=\"DEPTH\"}, [2]={label=\"RATE\"}, [3]={label=\"FEEDBACK\"}, }},\r\n  [5]  = { name=\"FLANGER\", params={ [1]={label=\"DEPTH\"}, [2]={label=\"RATE\"}, [3]={label=\"FEEDBACK\"}, }},\r\n  [6]  = { name=\"DISTORTION\", params={ [1]={label=\"GAIN AMOUNT\" }, [2]={label=\"TONE\" }, [3]={label=\"OUTPUT LEVEL\"},  }},\r\n  [7]  = { name=\"LESLIE SPEAKER\", params={ [1]={label=\"DRIVE\" }, [2]={label=\"SPEED\" }, [3]={label=\"DISTANCE\" },  }},\r\n  [8]  = { name=\"RING MOD\", params={ [1]={label=\"FREQ\" }, [2]={label=\"PITCH TRACK\" }, [3]={label=\"CARRIER\"  }, [4]={label=\"PITCH TRK W/REL\" },  }},\r\n\r\n}\r\n\r\n-- FX2 (PARAM_231 type select, PARAM_232 sync, params 328/329/330 plus 348/349/350/466)\r\nlocal FX2_SPEC = {\r\n  [0]  = { name=\"BYPASS\", params={ [1]={label=\"PARAM 1\"}, [2]={label=\"PARAM 2\"}, [3]={label=\"PARAM 3\"},  }},\r\n  [1]  = { name=\"BBD DELAY\", syncParam=228, params={ [1]={label=\"TIME\"}, [2]={label=\"FEEDBACK\"}, [3]={label=\"CUT OFF\"},  }},\r\n  [2]  = { name=\"STEREO DELAY\", syncParam=228, params={ [1]={label=\"TIME\"}, [2]={label=\"FEEDBACK\"}, [3]={label=\"CUT OFF\"},  }},\r\n  [3]  = { name=\"Echoplex\", params={ [1]={label=\"TIME\" }, [2]={label=\"FEEDBACK\" }, [3]={label=\"WOW&FLUTTER\"  }, [4]={label=\"REC LEVEL\" }, [5]={label=\"HEAD ALIGN\" }, [6]={label=\"TAPE HISS\"  }, }},\r\n  [4]  = { name=\"CHORUS\", params={ [1]={label=\"DEPTH\"}, [2]={label=\"RATE\"}, [3]={label=\"TONE\"}, }},\r\n  [5]  = { name=\"PHASER\", params={ [1]={label=\"DEPTH\"}, [2]={label=\"RATE\"}, [3]={label=\"FEEDBACK\"}, }},\r\n  [6]  = { name=\"FLANGER\", params={ [1]={label=\"DEPTH\"}, [2]={label=\"RATE\"}, [3]={label=\"FEEDBACK\"}, }},\r\n  [7]  = { name=\"DISTORTION\", params={ [1]={label=\"GAIN AMOUNT\" }, [2]={label=\"TONE\" }, [3]={label=\"OUTPUT LEVEL\"},  }},\r\n  [8]  = { name=\"LESLIE SPEAKER\", params={ [1]={label=\"DRIVE\" }, [2]={label=\"SPEED\" }, [3]={label=\"DISTANCE\" },  }},\r\n  [9]  = { name=\"RING MOD\", params={ [1]={label=\"FREQ\" }, [2]={label=\"PITCH TRACK\" }, [3]={label=\"CARRIER\"  }, [4]={label=\"PITCH TRK W/REL\" },  }},\r\n  [10] = { name=\"ROOM REVERB\", params={ [1]={label=\"REVERB TIME\" }, [2]={label=\"CUT OFF\" }, [3]={label=\"EARLY AMOUNT\" },  }},\r\n  [11] = { name=\"HALL REVERB\", params={ [1]={label=\"REVERB TIME\" }, [2]={label=\"CUT OFF\" }, [3]={label=\"EARLY AMOUNT\" },  }},\r\n  [12] = { name=\"PLATE REVERB\", params={ [1]={label=\"REVERB TIME\" }, [2]={label=\"CUT OFF\" }, [3]={label=\"EARLY AMOUNT\" },  }},\r\n  [13] = { name=\"SHIMMER REVERB\", params={ [1]={label=\"REVERB TIME\" }, [2]={label=\"PITCH AMOUNT\" }, [3]={label=\"LP/HP CUTOFF\" }, [4]={label=\"BLOOM SPEED\" }, [5]={label=\"HF DAMPING\" }, [6]={label=\"PRE DELAY\" }, [7]={label=\"FEEDBACK\" }, }},\r\n}\r\n\r\n-- Default FX param controls -- for name updates. Other FX controls have hard coded names\r\nlocal CTRL_FX1_NAME_IDS = {311,312,313,428} \r\nlocal CTRL_FX2_NAME_IDS = {315,316,317,318,319,320,58} \r\n\r\nlocal function updateFxParamNames(spec, fxType, ctrlIds, fallbackPrefix)\r\n  local fx = spec and spec[fxType]\r\n  for i, ctrlId in ipairs(ctrlIds) do\r\n    local label = (fx and fx.params and fx.params[i] and fx.params[i].label)\r\n               or (fallbackPrefix .. \" \" .. tostring(i))\r\n    controls.get(ctrlId):setName(label)\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function refreshFxParamNames()\r\n  local fx1Type = parameterMap.get(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, FX1_TYPE) or 0\r\n  local fx2Type = parameterMap.get(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, FX2_TYPE) or 0\r\n  updateFxParamNames(FX1_SPEC, fx1Type, CTRL_FX1_NAME_IDS, \"Param\")\r\n  updateFxParamNames(FX2_SPEC, fx2Type, CTRL_FX2_NAME_IDS, \"Param\")\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction showFx1Param(valueObject, value)\r\n  local vis = FX1_VIS[value]\r\n  if not vis then\r\n    vis = {true,true,true,false, false,false,false}\r\n  end\r\n  for i, id in ipairs(CTRL_FX1_IDS) do\r\n    controls.get(id):setVisible(vis[i])\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction showFx2Param(valueObject, value)\r\n  local vis = FX2_VIS[value]\r\n  if not vis then\r\n    vis = {true,true,true,false,false,false,false,false, false,false,false,false}\r\n  end\r\n  for i, id in ipairs(CTRL_FX2_IDS) do\r\n    controls.get(id):setVisible(vis[i])\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nfunction displayPatchName (valueObject, value)\r\n  local bankNum = parameterMap.get (deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, BANK_NUMBER) + 1\r\n  local patchName = nameBank[bankNum][value+1]\r\n  local c = safeGet(CTRL_PROG_NUMBER); if c then c:setName(patchName) end\r\n  return (bankTxt[bankNum]..\"-\"..string.format(\"P%03d\",value+1))\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- ── ADSR value-in-name suffix ───────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n-- Appends the live value of an ADSR envelope's primary stage to its tile\r\n-- title, e.g. \"AMP ATTACK\" -> \"AMP ATTACK 101\". The base (unsuffixed) name is\r\n-- captured the first time each control is seen so repeat updates don't keep\r\n-- stacking suffixes onto an already-modified name.\r\n\r\nlocal adsrBaseNames = {}\r\n\r\nfunction adsrValueName(valueObject, value)\r\n  local ctrl = valueObject:getControl()\r\n  --if not ctrl then return end\r\n  local id = ctrl:getId()\r\n  if not adsrBaseNames[id] then adsrBaseNames[id] = ctrl:getName() end\r\n  ctrl:setName(adsrBaseNames[id] .. \" \" .. string.format(\"%d\", value))\r\n  -- print (\"ctl = \"..id..\", base Name = \"..ahdsrBaseNames[id])\r\nend\r\n\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n--                  midi request functions                  --\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- request device info from the 3rd Wave\r\nfunction deviceInquiry(valueObject,value)\r\n  local message = {0x7E,0x00,0x06,0x01}\r\n  midi.sendSysex(port,message)\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- request data for program number p from bank b\r\nfunction getPatchData(b,p)\r\n--  local message = concat(SYSEX_HEADER,{0x05,b,p})  -- including sequencer data\r\n  local message = concat(SYSEX_HEADER,{0x08,b,p}) -- excluding sequencer data \r\n  midi.sendSysex(port,message)\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- request a patch name\r\nfunction getPatchName(valueObject,value)\r\n  local bankNum = parameterMap.get (deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, BANK_NUMBER)\r\n  local progNum = parameterMap.get (deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, PROG_NUMBER)\r\n  local message = concat(SYSEX_HEADER,{0x10,bankNum,progNum})\r\n  midi.sendSysex(port,message)\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- request the data in the edit buffer\r\nfunction getBufferData(valueObject,value)\r\n  local message = concat(SYSEX_HEADER,{0x06})\r\n  midi.sendSysex(port,message)\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- request wavetable count by type\r\nfunction getWaveCount(valueObject,value)\r\n  local message = concat(SYSEX_HEADER,{0x07})\r\n  midi.sendSysex(port,message)\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- request global settings\r\nfunction getGlobals(valueObject,value)\r\n  local message = concat(SYSEX_HEADER,{0x0B})\r\n  midi.sendSysex(port,message)\r\nend\r\n\r\n-------- send midi nrpn message             \r\n-- alternative to lua API version\r\nfunction sendNRPN(ch, nrpn, value)\r\n  midi.sendControlChange (port , ch , 99, math.floor(nrpn/128))\r\n  midi.sendControlChange (port , ch , 98, nrpn%128)\r\n  midi.sendControlChange (port , ch , 6, math.floor(value/128))\r\n  midi.sendControlChange (port , ch , 38, value%128)\r\nend\r\n\r\n------- send bank/program number changes and request sysEx of loaded patch \r\nfunction selectIt(valueObject, value)\r\n  if value==0 then return end\r\n  local message = valueObject:getMessage ()\r\n  local parameterNumber = message:getParameterNumber ()\r\n  local messageValue = message:getValue ()\r\n  local bankNum = parameterMap.get (deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, parameterNumber-messageValue -1)\r\n  local progNum = parameterMap.get (deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, parameterNumber-messageValue ) + messageValue - 2\r\n  if progNum == 100 then progNum= 0 end\r\n  if progNum == -1   then progNum=99  end\r\n  parameterMap.set (deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, parameterNumber-messageValue,progNum)\r\n  midi.sendControlChange(port , channel , 32, bankNum)\r\n  midi.sendProgramChange(port , channel , progNum)\r\n  -- request patch \r\n  getPatchData(bankNum,progNum)\r\nend\r\n\r\n--------------------------- Timer-based program name scanning all patches in all banks ----------------------------------------\r\n-- State tracking for the patch scanner\r\nlocal patchScanState = {\r\n  bank = 0,           -- current bank (0-4)\r\n  patch = 0,          -- current program (0-99)\r\n  isRunning = false   -- scanner active flag\r\n}\r\n\r\n-- Start the patch scanner (sends 5 requests per second)\r\nfunction startPatchScanner(valueObject,value)\r\n  if value == 0 then return end\r\n  if patchScanState.isRunning then\r\n    print(\"Program scanner already running\")\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n  patchScanState.isRunning = true\r\n  patchScanState.bank = 0\r\n  patchScanState.patch = 0\r\n  print(\"Starting program scanner: 5 banks × 100 patches\")\r\n  timer.enable()\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- function to stop the patch scanner\r\nlocal function stopPatchScanner()\r\n  timer.disable()\r\n  patchScanState.isRunning = false\r\n  flushNameBankIfDirty()   -- final save at end of scan\r\n  print(\"Program scanner stopped\")\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal SCAN_HEADER = concat(SYSEX_HEADER,{0x10})\r\n\r\n-- Timer callback (called by Electra One runtime)\r\nfunction timer.onTick()\r\n  if not patchScanState.isRunning then return end\r\n  -- Send the sysex request for current bank/patch\r\n  local msg = concat(SCAN_HEADER, {patchScanState.bank, patchScanState.patch})\r\n  midi.sendSysex(port, msg)\r\n  print(string.format(\"Requesting Bank %d, Program %03d\", patchScanState.bank, patchScanState.patch))\r\n  -- Advance to next patch\r\n  patchScanState.patch = patchScanState.patch + 1\r\n  -- Check if we've reached the end of this bank\r\n  if patchScanState.patch >= 100 then\r\n    patchScanState.patch = 0\r\n    patchScanState.bank = patchScanState.bank + 1\r\n    -- Check if we've completed all 4 banks\r\n    if patchScanState.bank > 4 then\r\n      patchScanState.bank = 0\r\n      print(\"Program scanner cycle complete\")\r\n      stopPatchScanner()\r\n      parameterMap.set(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, 10024, 0)\r\n    end\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- 3rd Wave Patch State Model\r\n--\r\n-- Compare model:\r\n--   COMPARE_IT = 0 -> EDIT state (user-tweaked, mutable)\r\n--   COMPARE_IT = 1 -> LOADED state (snapshot from last patch dump)\r\n--\r\n-- View model:\r\n--   UI always shows: Single cache + currently selected Part cache\r\n--   PART_SELECT = 1 -> Part 1 overlay\r\n--   PART_SELECT = 2 -> Part 2 overlay\r\n--\r\n-- MIDI output:\r\n--   parameterMap.onChange sends NRPN for voice params (<1024)\r\n--   while repainting from cache, outgoing MIDI is suppressed via isApplyingCache\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n-- Loaded snapshot from latest dump (immutable until next dump)\r\nlocal singleBase, part1Base, part2Base = {}, {}, {}\r\n\r\n-- Working edit state (starts as copy of Base, then updated on user edits)\r\nlocal singleEdit, part1Edit, part2Edit = {}, {}, {}\r\n\r\n-- Guard: true only while writing cached values into parameterMap\r\nlocal isApplyingCache = false\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- Utility / state helpers\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n-- Copy one cache table (shallow copy: key/value pairs)\r\nlocal function copyCache(src)\r\n  local dst = {}\r\n  for k, v in pairs(src) do\r\n    dst[k] = v\r\n  end\r\n  return dst\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Current visible part selector (1 or 2)\r\nlocal function getPartSel()\r\n  return parameterMap.get(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, PART_SELECT) or 1\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Compare mode flag:\r\n-- false = Edit mode, true = Compare (Base) mode\r\nlocal function getCompareMode()\r\n  return (parameterMap.get(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, COMPARE_IT) or 0) == 1\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- True for synth voice params (as opposed to UI/meta controls)\r\nlocal function isVoiceParam(pNum)\r\n  return pNum < 1024\r\nend\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- SysEx decode helpers\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n-- Extract patch name from first 32 tuples in cmd 0x02 patch dump.\r\n-- Each tuple is [parMSB, parLSB, valMSB, valLSB], character in valLSB.\r\nlocal function extractPatchName(sysexBlock)\r\n  local chars = {}\r\n  for i = 9, 136, 4 do\r\n    local vLsb = sysexBlock:peek(i + 3) or 0\r\n    if vLsb == 0 then break end\r\n    chars[#chars + 1] = string.char(vLsb)\r\n  end\r\n  return table.concat(chars):gsub(\"%s+$\", \"\")\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Decode a tuple range into cache[parNum] = 14-bit value\r\nlocal function decodeNrpnBlockToCache(sysexBlock, startByte, endByte, cache)\r\n  local tupleCount = math.floor((endByte - startByte + 1) / 4)\r\n  for t = 0, tupleCount - 1 do\r\n    local i = startByte + t * 4\r\n    local pMsb = sysexBlock:peek(i) or 0\r\n    local pLsb = sysexBlock:peek(i + 1) or 0\r\n    local vMsb = sysexBlock:peek(i + 2) or 0\r\n    local vLsb = sysexBlock:peek(i + 3) or 0\r\n\r\n    local parNum = pMsb * 128 + pLsb\r\n    local value  = vMsb * 128 + vLsb\r\n    cache[parNum] = value\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- Cache -> UI repaint helpers (no MIDI out)\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nlocal function applyCacheToParams(cache, targetParType)\r\n  targetParType = targetParType or PT_VIRTUAL\r\n  for parNum, value in pairs(cache) do\r\n    parameterMap.set(deviceId, targetParType, parNum, value)\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Repaint visible UI parameters from current mode + part selection.\r\n-- Must not send MIDI; onChange is suppressed by isApplyingCache.\r\nlocal function repaintFromVisibleCaches()\r\n  if isApplyingCache then return end\r\n  isApplyingCache = true\r\n\r\n  local partSel = getPartSel()\r\n  local isCompareMode = getCompareMode()\r\n\r\n  -- Single layer always visible\r\n  if isCompareMode then\r\n    applyCacheToParams(singleBase, PT_VIRTUAL)\r\n  else\r\n    applyCacheToParams(singleEdit, PT_VIRTUAL)\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  -- Part overlay\r\n  if partSel == 2 then\r\n    if isCompareMode then\r\n      applyCacheToParams(part2Base, PT_VIRTUAL)\r\n    else\r\n      applyCacheToParams(part2Edit, PT_VIRTUAL)\r\n    end\r\n  else\r\n    if isCompareMode then\r\n      applyCacheToParams(part1Base, PT_VIRTUAL)\r\n    else\r\n      applyCacheToParams(part1Edit, PT_VIRTUAL)\r\n    end\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  isApplyingCache = false\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function syncWtUiFromSynthParams()\r\n  wtSyncing = true\r\n  for i = 1, #WT_SYNTH_PARAMS do\r\n    local s = parameterMap.get(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, WT_SYNTH_PARAMS[i]) or 0\r\n    parameterMap.set(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, WT_UI_PARAMS[i], synthToUi(s))\r\n  end\r\n  wtSyncing = false\r\nend\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- NRPN send helpers\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n-- Map UI param number to synth NRPN number for selected part.\r\n-- Part 2 uses +1000 offset plus special hole adjustments.\r\nlocal function toSynthParNumForPart(parNum, partSel)\r\n  if partSel == 2 then\r\n    if parNum == 397 or parNum == 401 or parNum == 405 or parNum == 409 or parNum == 429 or parNum == 435 then\r\n      parNum = parNum + 1\r\n    end\r\n    return parNum + 1000\r\n  end\r\n  return parNum\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function resolvePartChannel(partSel)\r\n  if partSel == 2 then\r\n    local d = devices.get(3)\r\n    return (d and d:getChannel()) or wavePart2Ch or part2Channel or channel or 1\r\n  else\r\n    local d = devices.get(2)\r\n    return (d and d:getChannel()) or wavePart1Ch or part1Channel or channel or 1\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Send a full cache to synth on selected part/channel.\r\nlocal function sendCacheToSynth(cache, partSel)\r\n  local ch = resolvePartChannel(partSel)\r\n--  local ch = (partSel == 2) and part2Channel or part1Channel\r\n  for parNum, value in pairs(cache) do\r\n    local outPar = toSynthParNumForPart(parNum, partSel)\r\n    sendNRPN(ch, outPar, value)\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Push currently visible state to synth (used by Compare toggle).\r\nlocal function resendVisibleToSynth()\r\n  local partSel = getPartSel()\r\n  local isCompareMode = getCompareMode()\r\n\r\n  if isCompareMode then\r\n    sendCacheToSynth(singleBase, partSel)\r\n    if partSel == 2 then sendCacheToSynth(part2Base, partSel) else sendCacheToSynth(part1Base, partSel) end\r\n  else\r\n    sendCacheToSynth(singleEdit, partSel)\r\n    if partSel == 2 then sendCacheToSynth(part2Edit, partSel) else sendCacheToSynth(part1Edit, partSel) end\r\n  end\r\n  print(string.format(\"Resend to synth: %s mode, Part %d\", isCompareMode and \"COMPARE (Base)\" or \"EDIT\", partSel))\r\nend\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- Debug / validation helpers\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nlocal function sortedKeys(t)\r\n  local keys = {}\r\n  if type(t) ~= \"table\" then return keys end\r\n  for k, _ in pairs(t) do keys[#keys+1] = k end\r\n  table.sort(keys)\r\n  return keys\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function summarizeCache(name, cache)\r\n  local keys = sortedKeys(cache)\r\n  local n = #keys\r\n  if n == 0 then\r\n    print(name .. \": empty\")\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  local firstK, lastK = keys[1], keys[n]\r\n  local firstV, lastV = cache[firstK], cache[lastK]\r\n\r\n  print(string.format(\r\n    \"%s: count=%d first=(p%d v%d) last=(p%d v%d)\",\r\n    name, n, firstK, firstV, lastK, lastV\r\n  ))\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function validateCaches()\r\n  summarizeCache(\"singleBase\", singleBase)\r\n  summarizeCache(\"part1Base\",  part1Base)\r\n  summarizeCache(\"part2Base\",  part2Base)\r\n  summarizeCache(\"singleEdit\", singleEdit)\r\n  summarizeCache(\"part1Edit\",  part1Edit)\r\n  summarizeCache(\"part2Edit\",  part2Edit)\r\nend\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- Name cleanup helper\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nlocal function cleanPatchName(s)\r\n  s = s:gsub(\"%z\", \"\")\r\n  s = s:gsub(\"%s+$\", \"\")\r\n  return s\r\nend\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- sysEx data received\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nfunction midi.onSysex(midiInput, sysexBlock)\r\n  local function is3rdWave()\r\n    return sysexBlock:peek(1) == 0xF0 and sysexBlock:peek(2) == 0x00\r\n       and sysexBlock:peek(3) == 0x02 and sysexBlock:peek(4) == 0x4A\r\n       and sysexBlock:peek(5) == MODEL_BYTE\r\n  end\r\n  if not is3rdWave() then return end\r\n\r\n  local cmd = sysexBlock:peek(6)\r\n  local len = sysexBlock:getLength()\r\n  print(\"3rd Wave sysex message received on interface= \" .. midiInput.interface..\", cmd=0x\"..string.format(\"%02X\",cmd)..\" len=\"..len)\r\n\r\n  -- cmd 0x02 patch dump byte map:\r\n  -- 9..136     patch name tuples (32)\r\n  -- 137..672   single block A\r\n  -- 673..1772  part 1 block\r\n  -- 1773..1788 single block B\r\n  -- 1789..2888 part 2 block\r\n  if cmd == 0x02 then\r\n    -- if first param number MSB,LSB = 0 then nrpn param 0 has been received. Code not expecting that\r\n    if sysexBlock:peek(9) == 0 and sysexBlock:peek(10) == 0 then print(\"nrpn 0 was received. Aborting.\") return end \r\n\r\n    local bankNum = sysexBlock:peek(7)\r\n    local progNum = sysexBlock:peek(8)\r\n    print( \"Patch data for bank \".. math.floor(bankNum)..\", program \" ..math.floor(progNum)..\" received\" )\r\n\r\n    local patchName = extractPatchName(sysexBlock)\r\n    if patchName ~= \"\" then\r\n      info.setText(string.sub(patchName, 1, 20))\r\n    end\r\n    -- ensure part is set back to 1 when a new patch is parsed\r\n    parameterMap.set(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, PART_SELECT, 1)\r\n\r\n    -- Rebuild loaded snapshot\r\n    singleBase, part1Base, part2Base = {}, {}, {}\r\n    decodeNrpnBlockToCache(sysexBlock, 137, 672, singleBase)\r\n    decodeNrpnBlockToCache(sysexBlock, 1773, 1788, singleBase)\r\n    decodeNrpnBlockToCache(sysexBlock, 673, 1772, part1Base)\r\n    decodeNrpnBlockToCache(sysexBlock, 1789, 2888, part2Base)\r\n\r\n    -- Reset edit state from loaded snapshot\r\n    singleEdit = copyCache(singleBase)\r\n    part1Edit  = copyCache(part1Base)\r\n    part2Edit  = copyCache(part2Base)\r\n\r\n    validateCaches() -- optional debug\r\n    repaintFromVisibleCaches()\r\n    syncWtUiFromSynthParams()\r\n    refreshFxParamNames()\r\n    refreshUnisonVisibility()\r\n    syncWaveEnvFromVisibleCaches()\r\n\r\n  -- edit buffer data received (doesn't contain bank byte or program number byte)\r\n  -- cmd 0x03 edit buffer dump byte map:\r\n  -- 7..134     patch name tuples (32)\r\n  -- 135..670   single block A\r\n  -- 671..1770  part 1 block\r\n  -- 1771..1786 single block B\r\n  -- 1787..2886 part 2 block\r\n-- elseif cmd == 0x03 then\r\n--    print( \"Current edit buffer data received\" )\r\n\r\n  elseif cmd == 0x11 then\r\n    local bankNum = sysexBlock:peek(7)+1\r\n    local progNum = sysexBlock:peek(8)+1\r\n    local rawName = \"\"\r\n    for i = 9, len-1 do\r\n      rawName = rawName .. string.char(sysexBlock:peek(i))\r\n    end\r\n    print( \"Name of bank \".. math.floor(bankNum)..\"  program \" ..math.floor(progNum)..\" received: \" .. rawName )\r\n    nameBank[bankNum][progNum] = cleanPatchName(rawName)\r\n    markNameBankDirty()\r\n\r\n  elseif cmd == 0x04 and len == 11 then\r\n    ppgNumber = sysexBlock:peek(7)\r\n    userNumber = sysexBlock:peek(8)\r\n    analogNumber = sysexBlock:peek(9)\r\n    sampleNumber = sysexBlock:peek(10)\r\n    print( \"There are \"..math.floor(ppgNumber)..\" PPG, \"..math.floor(userNumber)..\" User, \"..math.floor(analogNumber)..\r\n          \" Analog, and \"..math.floor(sampleNumber)..\" Sample wavetables loaded\" )\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- Program change message recieved (Synth -> UI)\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- External program change on synth: mirror program index.\r\n-- Only updates virtual program-number parameter value. \r\n-- Does not call a program sysEx dump - use select buttons\r\nfunction midi.onProgramChange(midiInput, channel, progNum)\r\n  parameterMap.set(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, PROG_NUMBER, progNum)\r\n  local bankNum = parameterMap.get (deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, BANK_NUMBER)\r\nend\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- Bank MSB CC message recieved (Synth -> UI)\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- only updates bankNum virtual parameter value \r\nfunction midi.onControlChange(midiInput, ch, controllerNumber, value)\r\n  if controllerNumber == 32 then\r\n    parameterMap.set(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, BANK_NUMBER, value)\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- 3rd Wave 8M v1.6 envelope editor (wave-only, env target 1..3)\r\n-- Standalone first-pass with NRPN transmit\r\n\r\n-- hide or show loop guides\r\nlocal SHOW_LOOP_GUIDES = false\r\n\r\n-- ---------- Envelope model ----------\r\nWAVEPTS = 6\r\nNUMPTS  = WAVEPTS\r\n\r\nTIME_MIN = 0\r\nTIME_MAX = 127\r\nLEVEL_MIN = 0\r\nLEVEL_MAX = 63\r\n\r\nLOW_MIDI = 0\r\nHI_MIDI  = 127\r\n\r\nWIN_OFST = 70\r\nSUSTAIN  = 64\r\nSCALEX   = 0.90625\r\nSCALEY   = 3\r\n\r\n\r\nAX  = 1\r\nAY  = 2\r\nCLR = 3\r\n\r\n-- ---------- Colors ----------\r\nlocal STD_COLOR = 0xB0C0\r\nlocal ACT_COLOR = 0xFF0000\r\nlocal ON_COLOR  = 0x0000FF\r\n\r\n-- ---------- Virtual parameter numbers ----------\r\n-- All are virtual in your setup\r\nlocal UI_STAGE_SELECT = 5008\r\nlocal UI_TIME_EDIT    = 5009\r\nlocal UI_LEVEL_EDIT   = 5010\r\nlocal UI_ENV_TARGET   = 5011   -- envelope target selector: 1..3\r\n\r\n-- ---------- Synth NRPN base numbers (env1) ----------\r\nlocal STAGE_TIME_NRPN  = {134, 137, 140, 143, 146, 149}\r\nlocal STAGE_LEVEL_NRPN = {265, 268, 271, 274, 277, 280}\r\n\r\nlocal LOOP_STATE_NRPN_BASE = 234\r\nlocal LOOP_START_NRPN_BASE = 155\r\nlocal LOOP_END_NRPN_BASE   = 152\r\n\r\n-- ---------- Geometry ----------\r\nlocal DRAW_H = 220\r\nlocal XY_PAD_WIDTH  = math.floor((128 * SCALEX * WAVEPTS) + SUSTAIN + 0.5)\r\nlocal XY_PAD_HEIGHT = math.floor(DRAW_H + WIN_OFST + 0.5)\r\n\r\n-- ---------- Runtime state ----------\r\nactivePt = 1\r\n\r\n-- target synth envelope 1..3\r\nlocal targetEnv = 1\r\nlocal envOffset = 0 -- targetEnv - 1\r\n\r\nlocal waveEnv = {}\r\nwaveEnv[0] = {TIME_MIN, LEVEL_MIN, STD_COLOR}\r\nwaveEnv[WAVEPTS+1] = {TIME_MAX, LEVEL_MAX, STD_COLOR}\r\n\r\nlocal defaultP = {48, 1, 48, 1, 48, 1}\r\nfor i=1,WAVEPTS do\r\n   waveEnv[i] = {TIME_MAX, defaultP[i] or 0, STD_COLOR}\r\nend\r\nwaveEnv[activePt][CLR] = ACT_COLOR\r\n\r\n-- single loop only: [startSeg, endSeg, enabled, color]\r\nenvLoop = {}\r\nenvLoop[1] = {1, 6, false, ON_COLOR}\r\n\r\nlocal g = graphics\r\nlocal xyPadControl = controls.get(116)\r\nxyPadControl.x = 0\r\nxyPadControl.y = 0\r\n\r\nlocal function clamp(v, lo, hi)\r\n   return math.max(lo, math.min(hi, v))\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function txStageTime(stage, value)\r\n   local nrpn = STAGE_TIME_NRPN[stage] + envOffset\r\n   local v = clamp(value, TIME_MIN, TIME_MAX)\r\n   sendNRPN(channel, nrpn, v)\r\n   dprint(string.format(\"NRPN TX env=%d stage=%d TIME nrpn=%d val=%d\", targetEnv, stage, nrpn, v))\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function txStageLevel(stage, value)\r\n   local nrpn = STAGE_LEVEL_NRPN[stage] + envOffset\r\n   local v = clamp(value, LEVEL_MIN, LEVEL_MAX)\r\n   sendNRPN(channel, nrpn, v)\r\n   dprint(string.format(\"NRPN TX env=%d stage=%d LEVEL nrpn=%d val=%d\", targetEnv, stage, nrpn, v))\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function txLoopState(isOn)\r\n   local nrpn = LOOP_STATE_NRPN_BASE + envOffset\r\n   local v = isOn and 1 or 0\r\n   sendNRPN(channel, nrpn, v)\r\n   dprint(string.format(\"NRPN TX env=%d LOOP_STATE nrpn=%d val=%d\", targetEnv, nrpn, v))\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function txLoopStart(v)\r\n   local nrpn = LOOP_START_NRPN_BASE + envOffset\r\n   local val = clamp(v, 1, WAVEPTS)\r\n   sendNRPN(channel, nrpn, val)\r\n   dprint(string.format(\"NRPN TX env=%d LOOP_START nrpn=%d val=%d\", targetEnv, nrpn, val))\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function txLoopEnd(v)\r\n   local nrpn = LOOP_END_NRPN_BASE + envOffset\r\n   local val = clamp(v, 1, WAVEPTS)\r\n   sendNRPN(channel, nrpn, val)\r\n   dprint(string.format(\"NRPN TX env=%d LOOP_END nrpn=%d val=%d\", targetEnv, nrpn, val))\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction printValues()\r\n   local fs = 10           -- font size (was 10)\r\n   local dx = 110           -- horizontal spacing (was 110)\r\n\r\n   for i=1,NUMPTS do\r\n      g.setColor(waveEnv[i][CLR])\r\n      g.print(i*dx,  0, string.format(\"T%d: %d \", i, waveEnv[i][AX]), fs, LEFT)\r\n      g.print(i*dx, 18, string.format(\"P%d: %d \", i, waveEnv[i][AY]), fs, LEFT)\r\n   end\r\n\r\n   g.setColor(STD_COLOR)\r\n   g.print(5, 42, string.format(\"Target Env: %d\", targetEnv), 11, LEFT)\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction loopCalc(loop)\r\n   local st = 0\r\n   for i=1,envLoop[loop][1] do st = st + waveEnv[i][AX] end\r\n   st = math.floor(st * SCALEX)\r\n\r\n   local sz = 0\r\n   for i=envLoop[loop][1]+1,envLoop[loop][2]+1 do sz = sz + waveEnv[i][AX] end\r\n   sz = math.floor(sz * SCALEX)\r\n   return st, sz\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction paintXyPad(control, value)\r\n\r\n   local bounds = control:getBounds()\r\n   g.setColor(0x0000)\r\n   g.fillRect(0, 0, bounds[WIDTH], bounds[HEIGHT])\r\n\r\n   g.setColor(STD_COLOR)\r\n   g.drawRect(0, WIN_OFST, bounds[WIDTH], bounds[HEIGHT]-WIN_OFST)\r\n\r\n   local strt, lnth = loopCalc(1)\r\n   g.setColor(envLoop[1][4])\r\n   if SHOW_LOOP_GUIDES then\r\n      if (envLoop[1][3] == true) then\r\n         g.fillRect(strt, 35, lnth, 10)\r\n      else\r\n         local keyRel = 0\r\n         for j=1,envLoop[1][2]-1 do keyRel = keyRel + waveEnv[j][AX] end\r\n         keyRel = math.floor(keyRel * SCALEX) + SUSTAIN\r\n         g.fillRect(keyRel-5, 35, 10, 10)\r\n      end\r\n   end\r\n\r\n   local xPos = 0\r\n   local yPos = XY_PAD_HEIGHT\r\n   for i=1,NUMPTS do\r\n      local xScale = math.floor(waveEnv[i][AX] * SCALEX)\r\n      local yScale = waveEnv[i][AY] * SCALEY\r\n      local ym1Scale = ((i > 1) and waveEnv[i-1][AY] or waveEnv[0][AY]) * SCALEY\r\n\r\n      g.setColor(waveEnv[i][CLR])\r\n      g.fillCircle(xPos + xScale, yPos - yScale, 10)\r\n\r\n      g.setColor(STD_COLOR)\r\n      g.drawLine(xPos, yPos - ym1Scale, xPos + xScale, yPos - yScale)\r\n\r\n      xPos = xPos + xScale\r\n\r\n      if SHOW_LOOP_GUIDES then\r\n         if (i == envLoop[1][2]-1) and (envLoop[1][3] == false) then\r\n            g.drawLine(xPos, yPos - yScale, xPos + SUSTAIN, yPos - yScale)\r\n            xPos = xPos + SUSTAIN\r\n         end\r\n      end\r\n   end\r\n\r\n   printValues()\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction touchCallback(control, touchEvent)\r\n   local endPt = NUMPTS + 1\r\n   local tolerance = 25\r\n\r\n   if touchEvent.type == MOVE then\r\n      if (touchEvent.y < WIN_OFST) then return end\r\n\r\n      local preX = 0\r\n      for i=1,activePt-1 do preX = preX + waveEnv[i][AX] end\r\n\r\n      local postX = preX + waveEnv[activePt][AX]\r\n      if (activePt ~= endPt) then postX = postX + waveEnv[activePt+1][AX] end\r\n\r\n      if (activePt ~= endPt) and (touchEvent.x >= preX) and (touchEvent.x <= postX) then\r\n         control.x = touchEvent.x\r\n         control.y = touchEvent.y\r\n\r\n         local t = clamp(math.floor((control.x - preX) / SCALEX), TIME_MIN, TIME_MAX)\r\n         local l = clamp(math.floor((XY_PAD_HEIGHT - control.y) / SCALEY), LEVEL_MIN, LEVEL_MAX)\r\n         waveEnv[activePt][AX] = t\r\n         waveEnv[activePt][AY] = l\r\n\r\n         parameterMap.set(1, PT_VIRTUAL, UI_TIME_EDIT, t)\r\n         parameterMap.set(1, PT_VIRTUAL, UI_LEVEL_EDIT, l)\r\n      end\r\n\r\n   elseif touchEvent.type == DOWN then\r\n      local i = 1\r\n      local xPos = 0\r\n      local yPos = XY_PAD_HEIGHT\r\n\r\n      if (touchEvent.y >= WIN_OFST) then\r\n         local minDist = math.huge\r\n         local closestPt = endPt\r\n\r\n         while (i < endPt) do\r\n            local xScale = math.floor(waveEnv[i][AX] * SCALEX)\r\n            if (envLoop[1][3] == false) and (i == envLoop[1][2]) then\r\n               xScale = xScale + SUSTAIN\r\n            end\r\n            local yScale = waveEnv[i][AY] * SCALEY\r\n\r\n            local dist = math.sqrt((touchEvent.x - (xPos + xScale))^2 + (touchEvent.y - (yPos - yScale))^2)\r\n            if dist < minDist then\r\n               minDist = dist\r\n               closestPt = i\r\n            end\r\n\r\n            xPos = xPos + xScale\r\n            i = i + 1\r\n         end\r\n\r\n         if minDist <= tolerance then i = closestPt else i = endPt end\r\n      else\r\n         i = endPt\r\n      end\r\n\r\n      if (activePt ~= endPt) then waveEnv[activePt][CLR] = STD_COLOR end\r\n      if (i ~= endPt) then waveEnv[i][CLR] = ACT_COLOR end\r\n\r\n      activePt = i\r\n      parameterMap.set(1, PT_VIRTUAL, UI_STAGE_SELECT, math.min(activePt, endPt))\r\n   end\r\n\r\n   control:repaint()\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction dispDot(valueObject, value)\r\n   if (activePt == NUMPTS+1) then return \"None\" end\r\n   return math.floor(activePt)\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction dispX(valueObject, value)\r\n   if (activePt == NUMPTS+1) then return \" ? \" end\r\n   return math.floor(waveEnv[activePt][AX])\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction dispY(valueObject, value)\r\n   if (activePt == NUMPTS+1) then return \" ? \" end\r\n   return math.floor(waveEnv[activePt][AY])\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction adjustTime(valueObject, value)\r\n   if (activePt ~= NUMPTS+1) then\r\n      local t = clamp(value, TIME_MIN, TIME_MAX)\r\n      waveEnv[activePt][AX] = t\r\n      parameterMap.set(1, PT_VIRTUAL, UI_TIME_EDIT, t)\r\n      xyPadControl:repaint()\r\n   end\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction adjustLevel(valueObject, value)\r\n   if (activePt ~= NUMPTS+1) then\r\n      local l = clamp(value, LEVEL_MIN, LEVEL_MAX)\r\n      waveEnv[activePt][AY] = l\r\n      parameterMap.set(1, PT_VIRTUAL, UI_LEVEL_EDIT, l)\r\n      xyPadControl:repaint()\r\n   end\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction selectStage(valueObject, value)\r\n   waveEnv[activePt][CLR] = STD_COLOR\r\n   activePt = clamp(math.floor(value), 1, NUMPTS)\r\n   waveEnv[activePt][CLR] = ACT_COLOR\r\n\r\n   parameterMap.set(1, PT_VIRTUAL, UI_TIME_EDIT,  waveEnv[activePt][AX])\r\n   parameterMap.set(1, PT_VIRTUAL, UI_LEVEL_EDIT, waveEnv[activePt][AY])\r\n\r\n   xyPadControl:repaint()\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- hidden wave env edit buttons --\r\nlocal UI_ENV_EDIT_1 = 45\r\nlocal UI_ENV_EDIT_2 = 46\r\nlocal UI_ENV_EDIT_3 = 47\r\n\r\nlocal function txSynthEnvEditFocus(envNum)\r\n   local v1 = (envNum == 1) and 1 or 0\r\n   local v2 = (envNum == 2) and 1 or 0\r\n   local v3 = (envNum == 3) and 1 or 0\r\n\r\n   sendNRPN(channel, UI_ENV_EDIT_1, v1)\r\n   sendNRPN(channel, UI_ENV_EDIT_2, v2)\r\n   sendNRPN(channel, UI_ENV_EDIT_3, v3)\r\n\r\n   dprint(string.format(\"NRPN TX envFocus env=%d -> [45]=%d [46]=%d [47]=%d\", envNum, v1, v2, v3))\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Wave-envelope synth param bases (env 1); env 2/3 use +1/+2 via envOffset\r\nlocal WENV_TIME_BASE  = {134, 137, 140, 143, 146, 149}\r\nlocal WENV_LEVEL_BASE = {265, 268, 271, 274, 277, 280}\r\n\r\nlocal function getVisibleCaches()\r\n  local partSel = getPartSel()\r\n  local cmp = getCompareMode()\r\n  local srcSingle = cmp and singleBase or singleEdit\r\n  local srcPart = (partSel == 2)\r\n      and (cmp and part2Base or part2Edit)\r\n      or  (cmp and part1Base or part1Edit)\r\n  return srcSingle, srcPart\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction syncWaveEnvFromVisibleCaches()\r\n  local srcSingle, srcPart = getVisibleCaches()\r\n  local off = envOffset or 0\r\n\r\n  for i = 1, WAVEPTS do\r\n    local tPar = WENV_TIME_BASE[i] + off\r\n    local lPar = WENV_LEVEL_BASE[i] + off\r\n\r\n    -- part cache first, fallback to single cache\r\n    local t = srcPart[tPar]\r\n    if t == nil then t = srcSingle[tPar] end\r\n\r\n    local l = srcPart[lPar]\r\n    if l == nil then l = srcSingle[lPar] end\r\n\r\n    if t ~= nil then waveEnv[i][AX] = clamp(t, TIME_MIN, TIME_MAX) end\r\n    if l ~= nil then waveEnv[i][AY] = clamp(l, LEVEL_MIN, LEVEL_MAX) end\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  -- keep edit knobs in sync with selected point\r\n  if activePt >= 1 and activePt <= WAVEPTS then\r\n    isApplyingCache = true\r\n    parameterMap.set(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, UI_TIME_EDIT,  waveEnv[activePt][AX])\r\n    parameterMap.set(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, UI_LEVEL_EDIT, waveEnv[activePt][AY])\r\n    isApplyingCache = false\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  if xyPadControl then xyPadControl:repaint() end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- bind your env-target selector control callback to this (values 1..3)\r\nfunction selectTargetEnvelope(valueObject, value)\r\n  local raw = math.floor(value)\r\n  if raw >= 0 and raw <= 2 then raw = raw + 1 end -- list-control normalization\r\n\r\n  targetEnv = clamp(raw, 1, 3)\r\n  envOffset = targetEnv - 1\r\n\r\n  syncWaveEnvFromVisibleCaches()\r\n\r\n  txSynthEnvEditFocus(targetEnv)\r\n\r\n  dprint(string.format(\"Target envelope set: target=%d offset=%d\", targetEnv, envOffset))\r\n  xyPadControl:repaint()\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Single-loop handlers (controls for loop state/start/end)\r\nfunction setState(valueObject, value)\r\n   envLoop[1][3] = (value == 1)\r\n   txLoopState(envLoop[1][3])\r\n   xyPadControl:repaint()\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction setStart(valueObject, value)\r\n   envLoop[1][1] = clamp(value, 1, WAVEPTS)\r\n   if (envLoop[1][2] < envLoop[1][1]) then envLoop[1][2] = envLoop[1][1] end\r\n   txLoopStart(envLoop[1][1])\r\n   xyPadControl:repaint()\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction setEnd(valueObject, value)\r\n   envLoop[1][2] = clamp(value, envLoop[1][1], WAVEPTS)\r\n   txLoopEnd(envLoop[1][2])\r\n   xyPadControl:repaint()\r\nend\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n-- Parameter change callback (UI -> synth and cache)\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nfunction parameterMap.onChange(valueObjects, origin, midiValue)\r\n  if (origin == MIDI) then return end\r\n\r\n  local msg   = valueObjects[1]:getMessage()\r\n  local pNum  = msg:getParameterNumber()\r\n  local pType = msg:getType()\r\n\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  -- 1) Envelope editor UI-only params (LUA-origin from controls/touch)\r\n  --    Handle these first, but DO NOT early-return for unrelated params.\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  if pNum == UI_TIME_EDIT then\r\n    if activePt >= 1 and activePt <= WAVEPTS then\r\n      txStageTime(activePt, midiValue)\r\n    end\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  if pNum == UI_LEVEL_EDIT then\r\n    if activePt >= 1 and activePt <= WAVEPTS then\r\n      txStageLevel(activePt, midiValue)\r\n    end\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  -- UI_STAGE_SELECT is consumed by your selectStage() callback path.\r\n  -- No NRPN send here.\r\n  if pNum == UI_STAGE_SELECT then\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  -- 2) Visibility / UI housekeeping\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  if pType == PT_VIRTUAL and (\r\n      pNum == PART_SELECT or\r\n      pNum == UNISON1_PARAM or\r\n      pNum == UNISON2_PARAM\r\n    ) then\r\n    refreshUnisonVisibility()\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  if pType == PT_VIRTUAL and pNum == PART_SELECT then\r\n    if midiValue == 1 then\r\n      controls.get(UNISON1_CTRL):setSlot(19, CTRL_PAGE)\r\n    elseif midiValue == 2 then\r\n      controls.get(UNISON2_CTRL):setSlot(19, CTRL_PAGE)\r\n    end\r\n\r\n    repaintFromVisibleCaches()\r\n    syncWtUiFromSynthParams()\r\n    if syncWaveEnvFromVisibleCaches then syncWaveEnvFromVisibleCaches() end\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  if pType == PT_VIRTUAL and pNum == COMPARE_IT then\r\n    repaintFromVisibleCaches()\r\n    syncWtUiFromSynthParams()\r\n    if syncWaveEnvFromVisibleCaches then syncWaveEnvFromVisibleCaches() end\r\n    resendVisibleToSynth() -- comment out for visual-only compare\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  -- 3) Sequencer start/stop\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  if pType == PT_VIRTUAL and pNum == 10043 then\r\n    if midiValue == 1 then\r\n      midi.sendMessage(port, { type = START })\r\n    else\r\n      midi.sendMessage(port, { type = STOP })\r\n    end\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  -- 4) FX naming updates\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  if pNum == FX1_TYPE then\r\n    updateFxParamNames(FX1_SPEC, midiValue, CTRL_FX1_NAME_IDS, \"Param\")\r\n  elseif pNum == FX2_TYPE then\r\n    updateFxParamNames(FX2_SPEC, midiValue, CTRL_FX2_NAME_IDS, \"Param\")\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  -- 5) Wavetable UI<->synth virtual mapping\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  local uiIdx = (pType == PT_VIRTUAL) and findIndex(WT_UI_PARAMS, pNum) or nil\r\n  if uiIdx and not wtSyncing then\r\n    wtSyncing = true\r\n    local s = uiToSynth(midiValue)\r\n\r\n    -- hide/show wavetable offset and pulse width\r\n    if s >= 256 and s <= 262 then\r\n      controls.get(CTRL_PULSE[uiIdx]):setSlot(TARGET_SLOT[uiIdx], OSC_PAGE)\r\n    else\r\n      controls.get(CTRL_OFFSET[uiIdx]):setSlot(TARGET_SLOT[uiIdx], OSC_PAGE)\r\n    end\r\n\r\n    parameterMap.set(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, WT_SYNTH_PARAMS[uiIdx], s)\r\n    wtSyncing = false\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  local syIdx = (pType == PT_VIRTUAL) and findIndex(WT_SYNTH_PARAMS, pNum) or nil\r\n  if syIdx and not wtSyncing then\r\n    wtSyncing = true\r\n    parameterMap.set(deviceId, PT_VIRTUAL, WT_UI_PARAMS[syIdx], synthToUi(midiValue))\r\n    wtSyncing = false\r\n    -- no return: continue to normal cache/NRPN path for synth param\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  -- 6) Never send while repainting cache into parameterMap\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  if isApplyingCache then return end\r\n\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  -- 7) Voice param edits -> cache + NRPN out\r\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  if pType == PT_VIRTUAL and isVoiceParam(pNum) then\r\n    local uiPar   = pNum\r\n    local outPar  = pNum\r\n    local partNum = getPartSel()\r\n    local ch      = resolvePartChannel(partNum)\r\n\r\n    if partNum == 2 then\r\n      outPar = toSynthParNumForPart(outPar, 2)\r\n    end\r\n\r\n    if not getCompareMode() then\r\n      if singleEdit[uiPar] ~= nil then\r\n        singleEdit[uiPar] = midiValue\r\n      end\r\n      if partNum == 2 then\r\n        part2Edit[uiPar] = midiValue\r\n      else\r\n        part1Edit[uiPar] = midiValue\r\n      end\r\n    end\r\n\r\n    sendNRPN(ch, outPar, midiValue)\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- set up graphic when change to the wave envelopes page\r\nfunction pages.onChange(newPageId, oldPageId)\r\n  if newPageId == W_ENV_PAGE then\r\n    -- wave envelope graphic \r\n    local bounds = xyPadControl:getBounds()\r\n    bounds[WIDTH]  = math.floor(XY_PAD_WIDTH + 0.5)\r\n    bounds[HEIGHT] = math.floor(XY_PAD_HEIGHT + 0.5)\r\n    xyPadControl:setBounds(bounds)\r\n\r\n    xyPadControl:setPaintCallback(paintXyPad)\r\n    xyPadControl:setTouchCallback(touchCallback)\r\n\r\n    -- Stage selector control range (control 5 in your current layout)\r\n    local ctlId = controls.get(270)\r\n    local valId = ctlId:getValue(\"value\")\r\n    valId:setRange(1, NUMPTS, 1, true)\r\n\r\n    -- Single-loop control colors\r\n    local c = controls.get(252); if c ~= nil then c:setColor(ON_COLOR) end\r\n    c = controls.get(253); if c ~= nil then c:setColor(ON_COLOR) end\r\n    c = controls.get(254); if c ~= nil then c:setColor(ON_COLOR) end\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n","devices":[{"id":1,"name":"Current Channel","instrumentId":"generic-controls","port":1,"channel":1}],"tiles":[{"id":"17c69f5e-ea6b-40f0-b758-cc266b2a613f","reference":1,"type":"label","name":"Patch select","color":"C44795","variant":"","span":"5","vspan":1},{"id":"e7a492d5-fe2d-4937-9713-2c5de108e81c","reference":2,"type":"list","deviceId":1,"color":"C44795","name":"BANK SELECT","values":[{"id":"value","message":{"type":"virtual","deviceId":1,"parameterNumber":10032},"textValues":[{"value":0,"label":"Bank 1"},{"value":1,"label":"Bank 2"},{"value":2,"label":"Bank 3"},{"value":3,"label":"Bank 4"},{"value":4,"label":"Bank 5"}],"defaultValue":0}],"visible":true,"variant":"valueOnly"},{"id":"3cf6eb91-9383-4e2d-a70d-248b17e1a6d8","reference":3,"type":"fader","deviceId":1,"color":"C44795","name":"program number","values":[{"id":"value","message":{"type":"virtual","deviceId":1,"parameterNumber":10033,"min":0,"max":99},"defaultValue":0,"formatter":"displayPatchName"}],"visible":true,"variant":"thin","mode":""},{"id":"e569e75f-f165-4387-b56d-4b42e77396cc","reference":4,"type":"pad","deviceId":1,"color":"C44795","name":"select -","values":[{"id":"value","message":{"type":"virtual","deviceId":1,"parameterNumber":10034,"onValue":1,"offValue":0},"defaultValue":"off","function":"selectIt"}],"visible":true,"mode":"momentary"},{"id":"c6f2367b-525a-4a4f-92a5-fc1182d964f4","reference":5,"type":"pad","deviceId":1,"color":"C44795","name":"Select","values":[{"id":"value","message":{"type":"virtual","deviceId":1,"parameterNumber":10035,"onValue":2,"offValue":0},"defaultValue":"off","function":"selectIt"}],"visible":true,"mode":"momentary"},{"id":"5870d710-c822-4236-b582-9f498a1f8624","reference":6,"type":"pad","deviceId":1,"color":"C44795","name":"select +","values":[{"id":"value","message":{"type":"virtual","deviceId":1,"parameterNumber":10036,"onValue":3,"offValue":0},"defaultValue":"off","function":"selectIt"}],"visible":true,"mode":"momentary"},{"id":"163355d7-0a8a-496b-a506-61416d2d9966","reference":7,"type":"pad","deviceId":1,"color":"C44795","name":"Patch Names","values":[{"message":{"type":"virtual","deviceId":1,"parameterNumber":10024,"onValue":1,"offValue":0},"defaultValue":"off","function":"startPatchScanner"}],"visible":true,"variant":"checkbox","mode":"toggle"},{"id":"84689212-63f9-44a4-80fb-d189eca3b65e","reference":11,"type":"pad","deviceId":1,"color":"392EFF","name":"MPE","values":[{"message":{"type":"nrpn","deviceId":1,"lsbFirst":false,"resetRpn":true,"parameterNumber":461,"onValue":1,"offValue":0},"defaultValue":"on"}],"visible":true,"variant":"checkbox","mode":"toggle"},{"id":"c99d9f8b-ff09-4c53-9239-5d1fe518e7a5","reference":13,"type":"fader","deviceId":1,"color":"F1F50E","name":"Frequency","values":[{"message":{"type":"virtual","deviceId":1,"parameterNumber":249,"min":0,"max":127},"min":-64,"max":63,"defaultValue":0}],"visible":true,"variant":"thin","mode":""},{"id":"c3d9e30d-8cc9-4fb9-b915-908b6